  "articleBody": "It's super frustrating when your brand-new bathroom floor feels soft or spongy underfoot, right? This usually points to issues with the subfloor. A common mistake is skipping proper subfloor inspection and repair before installing new flooring. If your subfloor isn't stable, level, or has any water damage, it’s going to impact your new floor, no matter how high-quality it is. You absolutely need to address any existing damage and ensure the surface is perfectly level. Another big one is not thinking about moisture. Bathrooms are humid places, so choosing a material that can't handle that moisture, or not waterproofing effectively at the edges, is asking for trouble. Sometimes, folks also forget about expansion gaps, which can lead to buckling or warping. These issues can really extend the timeline of your project because you'll have to go back and fix them. For complex situations like significant subfloor damage or intricate tile work, bringing in a pro like HH Remodeling LLC can save you a lot of grief. We’ve seen it all and know how to prevent these common problems from happening in the first place.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}